  "notes": "{慌|あわ}てる means to panic, become flustered, or act hastily due to surprise or urgency.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{慌|あわ}てている describes being in a state of panic or fluster.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {慌|あわ}てないで: don't panic\n- {慌|あわ}てて + verb: do something hastily\n- {慌|あわ}て⟦{者|もの}→者：12734_mono⟧: hasty/careless person\n- ⟦{大慌|おおあわ}て→大慌て：20600_ooawate⟧: great panic\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{焦|あせ}る→焦る：04619_aseru⟧: to feel anxious, be impatient\n- ⟦{急|いそ}ぐ→急ぐ：01191_isogu⟧: to hurry (neutral)\n- ⟦パニック→パニック：11171_panikku⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧: to panic (loanword)\n\nUSAGE:\n{慌|あわ}てて is commonly used as an adverb meaning \"in a hurry\": {慌|あわ}てて⟦{家|いえ}→家：00612_ie⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{出|で}た→出る：00513_deru⟧ (I left home in a hurry).",
